## Introduction

This is the third piece of source material from the same external property (the Magnus Progenitor Saga / Biases as Constants, "MPS/BAC") scavenged for Telling Forward under the same rule established twice before in this repository: extract only the architecture and process signals that transfer, skip the property's own lore, characters, branding, and business decisions entirely. The pasted thread covers three things: a plan for book-by-book synopsis recovery (skipped — pure MPS/BAC content), a full "AI Council" tool-role-assignment strategy with a proposed Notion + GitHub content-operations architecture for migrating that project's canon (partially useful — concrete database/schema patterns, though its Notion-centric premise is the opposite of TF's confirmed direction), and a domain-name/release-title strategy for that property's own brand (skipped — no TF relevance). The material worth keeping is schema-level: a frontmatter standard, a term/glossary ledger schema, a revision/maturity-run ledger schema, and an AI-output provenance ledger schema — all of which give concrete field lists for two items TF already has open and undesigned (ADR-0005 item 2's provenance layer, ADR-0006 item 2's term/motif ledger).

## Extraction profile

- Depth: **balanced**, applied uniformly across the full paste.
- Focus: architecture/process/schema signals only, per this repository's standing scope rule. MPS/BAC narrative content, the book-synopsis planning turn, and the domain/title/brand/hardware/subscription-cost material were assessed and deliberately excluded as `omit-with-reason: out of scope for a Telling-Forward-only repository`.

