## Reusable assets

- Frontmatter field list (id, work_id, section_type, order, canon_layer, status, version, source_document, characters, motifs, canon_terms, github_path) — candidate baseline for TF scene/capsule markdown frontmatter.
- Term-ledger field list (term, definition, tier, casing rule, canon status, first appearance, drift risk, related entities, related motifs) — candidate baseline for ADR-0006 item 2's ledger.
- Provenance/revision field list (run type, maturity before/after [rung], issue type, tool used, accepted?, source commit/reference, source manuscript reference) — candidate baseline for ADR-0005 item 2's side-car provenance record.
- "Canon as Code" principle statement — candidate one-sentence addition to `docs/MISSION.md` or ADR-0001.
- Immutable raw-source rule statement — candidate addition to ADR-0004.
- Repo-splitting heuristic statement — candidate guidance note for whenever platform-code repo topology becomes a live question.

## Open questions

- Whether TF's `capsules` table design (still not started, per ADR-0004) should adopt any of the three field lists above wholesale, adapt them, or treat them only as loose inspiration — owner call, not decided by this extract.
- Whether a frontmatter standard belongs in this ADR track at all, or is better handled as a plain engineering spec once the capsule schema exists — flagged, not resolved here.
- The two attached PDFs were never actually read (not present in this session). If the owner wants deeper mining of the actual BAC Codex traceability-matrix mechanics beyond what ChatGPT summarized, that requires re-supplying the PDFs directly to a session with file access.

